{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he placed in basins.</b> Rashi: From here our Rabbis derived that our fathers entered the covenant of circumcision, immersion, and sprinkling of blood. And as for what we say in Yevamot, chapter HaCholetz, 'our fathers were circumcised but did not immerse' — one must say 'our fathers' there refers to Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob." "<b>He cast upon the altar.</b> Before he read to them the matters, and after he read to them he cast the other half of the blood upon the people."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "Chizkuni explicitly names Rashi here, which is unusual but not unheard of in his commentary."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:12.102842735Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}